    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a> </i></p><p><b>Emplacement Points:&nbsp;</b> 2</p><p><b>Size Restriction:&nbsp;</b> Gargantuan or Larger</p><p>Security Bracing entails a series of internal bulkheads and clamps designed to protect a section of a Starship- even if the ship as a whole is destroyed. Only <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Passenger_Conversions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Passenger Conversions\">Passenger Conversions</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Escape_Pods\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Escape Pods\">Escape Pods</a> can benefit from Security Bracing. When the ship reduced to 0 Hit Points by an attack that deals damage equal to or greater than its <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Damage_Threshold\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Damage Threshold\">Damage Threshold</a> (thus destroying the ship), subtract the ship's DR from the damage dealt to anyone in an area protected by Security Bracing. Anyone outside this area takes damage equal to one-half the amount that exceeded the ship's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Damage_Threshold\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Damage Threshold\">Damage Threshold</a>, as normal.</p><p>Security Bracing is common in big luxury liners and diplomatic transport vessels.</p>",
    "cost": "2000 (Base)",
